{"id":"9f6503267effd48c","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-thm-axiom-of-choice.md","title":"Axiom of Choice Equivalents","display":"thm-axiom-of-choice — Axiom of Choice Equivalents","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-axiom-of-choice","aliases":["58-thm-axiom-of-choice"],"display":"thm-axiom-of-choice — Axiom of Choice Equivalents","depends_on":["[[58-ax-ac]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-axiom-of-choice"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-axiom-of-choice</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-axiom-of-choice — Axiom of Choice Equivalents"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b3dac4cf78c440c7\" href=\"?note=b3dac4cf78c440c7\" title=\"58-ax-ac\">58-ax-ac</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function\">../batch16/58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AC}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{AC}_S\\)</span> (choice-axiom sentence defined below from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"b3dac4cf78c440c7\" href=\"?note=b3dac4cf78c440c7\" title=\"58-ax-ac\">58-ax-ac</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span> (set of nonempty sets)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (function predicate from dependency)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}axiom\\text{-}of\\text{-}choice\\text{-}sentence}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{AC}_S\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall F\\;\\Bigl(\n\\varnothing\\notin F\n\\to\\exists f\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(f,F,\\bigcup F)\n\\land\\forall A\\in F\\;(f(A)\\in A)\n\\bigr)\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}axiom\\text{-}of\\text{-}choice\\text{-}sentence}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{AC}_S\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall F\\;\\Bigl(\n\\varnothing\\notin F\n\\to\\exists f\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(f,F,\\bigcup F)\n\\land\\forall A\\in F\\;(f(A)\\in A)\n\\bigr)\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}axiom-of-choice}\\ \\vdash\\\n\\mathrm{AC}_S\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall F\\;\\Bigl(\n\\varnothing\\notin F\n\\to \\exists f\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(f,F,\\bigcup F)\n\\land \\forall A\\in F\\;(f(A)\\in A)\n\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}axiom-of-choice}\\ \\vdash\\\n\\mathrm{AC}_S\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall F\\;\\Bigl(\n\\varnothing\\notin F\n\\to \\exists f\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(f,F,\\bigcup F)\n\\land \\forall A\\in F\\;(f(A)\\in A)\n\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The symbol on the left is now explicitly linked to the sentence asserted by the axiom atom, rather than being an uninterpreted propositional constant.</li>\n<li>The axiom of choice is equivalent to the existence of a set-coded choice function on every set of nonempty sets.</li>\n<li>Many equivalent formulations: Zorn's lemma, well-ordering theorem, Tukey's lemma.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-ac","status":"resolved","id":"b3dac4cf78c440c7","anc